test: coverage wave 5 - lifecycle seams, crash arm, boundary tests (98.54% -> 98.72%)

+17 behaviour-asserting tests (695 lib / 810 total on Windows, 664 lib /
776 total on Linux), each carrying a Why: comment. Named residual
classes addressed:

- ollama runtime lifecycle: new injectable CommandRunner and
  InstallerRunner seams (background.rs CommandRunner pattern).
  start() delegates to start_with(executable, launch, attempts, poll):
  tests assert the exact launch contract (serve argument plus the six
  pinned environment entries), that a serving daemon is reused and never
  replaced, that reuse still enforces the supported-version floor, that a
  failed launch is attributed "Cannot start Ollama" with the cause
  preserved and no readiness wait, and that a runtime that never becomes
  ready fails on the injected schedule. install() delegates to
  install_with(run): the pinned winget contract (--id Ollama.Ollama
  --exact --source winget --accept-source-agreements
  --accept-package-agreements), refused-exit mapping and spawn-failure
  propagation are asserted, and a missing installer names the manual
  fallback. ollama.rs line misses 91 -> 48.
- worker panic arm: a panicking worker thread is proven to latch paused
  and stop, publish the typed fatal state and journal `worker_panicked`,
  observed through the runtime journal rather than sampled live state.
- engine error-attribution: update_settings runs the active enterprise
  policy before persisting - the policy clamp reaches the durable
  settings, and an unapproved model is refused and leaves the persisted
  settings untouched.
- store cursor/limit boundaries: malformed cursors (negative snapshot,
  zero progress, continuation past the high-water mark) are refused
  before any page work while the valid high-water edge is accepted; the
  1..=100 limit clamp holds on both feeds; next_cursor is set exactly at
  the limit+1 boundary and only there.
- diagnostics/shadow write_report tails via mock Write sinks: write-stage
  and flush-stage refusals propagate the sink's own error, an existing
  destination survives a refused overwrite, and shadow refuses a
  symlinked parent directory.
- recovery vault paths: export_recovery_key refuses a workspace whose
  live database does not authenticate under the active vault key, and no
  key file is written for it.

Windows line coverage (cargo llvm-cov --locked --all-features, summary
Lines column): 98.54% (479 missed / 32902) -> 98.72% (430 missed /
33465). Per-file misses: ollama.rs 91 -> 48, worker.rs 103 -> 98,
engine.rs 109 -> 108. docs/TESTING.md cites the new figure.

Residuals, documented per-line (line numbers at this commit):

- ollama.rs 1195-1198 (spawn_detached), 1285-1287 (install() wrapper),
  1331-1332 (system_installer real spawn): real OS-process launches,
  never executed by the suite by design (they would spawn a daemon or
  run the OS installer); their contracts are asserted through the
  injected runners. 1274: multi-line if-let closing-brace artifact.
  607-610 cold-profile unload deadline, 672-681 transport-recovery
  context arms, 693-694 verifier residency probe, 977-1032 analysis
  flag branches, 1112-1113 download-progress percent formatting: need
  deterministic cold/unload/GPU-loss runtime states or streamed progress
  fixtures (uncovered since earlier waves).
- engine.rs 1473 and 1552 `)?;` tails: unreachable defence-in-depth -
  auto_blocks re-checks analysis provenance and
  ensure_runtime_write_headroom guarantees runtime_write_safe before the
  duplicate dispatch_require runs. 612-615: real OAuth browser login.
  1013, 1707-1708: multi-line-statement closing-brace artifacts.
- store.rs 1162: test-helper guard arm (unreachable by construction);
  1794: SQL-failure tail of a state+revision CAS write (needs a corrupt
  store mid-transaction).
- recovery.rs 421, 1020: control-flow artifacts (loop break closing
  brace, cfg! branch closing brace); 1825: symlink-unsupported host
  fallback (platform capability).
- diagnostics.rs 307/313 (test closing-brace artifacts), 327/377
  (mock-responder catch-all arms for routes the product never requests);
  shadow.rs 542: symlink-unsupported host fallback.
- worker.rs 569-581: real ollama::install() fallback inside the
  InstallOllama dispatch (would launch the OS installer; the dispatch
  path itself is covered through the installer seam). Remaining run()
  timer-arm tails (retention failure backoff, scheduled-backup reschedule
  tails, local-ai and automatic circuit backoffs) need mid-operation
  storage or provider faults.
- gui.rs and tui.rs: rendering glue, per the coverage doctrine.

Gates: cargo test --locked green on Windows (695 lib / 810 total,
reconciled); cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D
warnings clean on Windows and Linux (Ubuntu-24.04, toolchain 1.99.0);
cargo fmt --all --check clean. Linux lane green on every suite except
tests/cli_workspace.rs tui_demo_mode_fails_fast_without_a_terminal,
which fails identically at clean HEAD 0d8ca7e in this WSL environment
(a controlling terminal is present there); not a change in this commit.
